251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (The Polling Booth System is a web-based application developed using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript with Local Storage for secure data handling. This system is designed to digitize and simplify the traditional polling process by allowing users to cast votes electronically in a controlled environment. It helps reduce manual effort, human errors, and time consumption during elections.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (The front end of the system is built using HTML for structure and CSS for designing a user-friendly interface. JavaScript is used to handle voting logic, voter verification, vote counting, and result generation. The Local Storage feature of the browser is used to store voter details, candidate data, and voting results without requiring an external database.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (The system ensures that each voter can vote only once by validating voter identity before allowing access to the voting panel. After successful voting, the vote is securely stored and automatically reflected in the result section. The admin module allows authorized users to view election results instantly.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (This project is cost-effective, easy to implement, and suitable for small-scale elections such as college elections, classroom voting, and organizational polls. It also helps students understand the practical implementation of front-end web technologies and client-side data storage.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Overall, the Polling Booth System provides a simple, secure, and efficient alternative to the traditional paper-based voting system.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
