322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 143 0 R
/T (INTRODUCTION)
/E (INTRODUCTION)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (In the early days, voting was done completely using manual methods where people marked their choice on ballot papers and dropped them into ballot boxes. After the completion of voting, the ballot boxes were opened and votes were counted manually. This process required a lot of time and human effort and was also highly prone to errors and manipulation. To reduce these problems, Electronic Voting Machines were introduced. EVMs reduced counting time and minimized human errors, but they still required physical presence and costly hardware equipment.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (With the development of computer networks and the internet, the concept of digital voting emerged. Online voting systems were developed to make the voting process more accessible and faster. These systems normally use web applications, databases, and authentication systems to conduct elections. However, developing such systems requires expensive servers and advanced security mechanisms. For educational institutions and small organizations, maintaining such complex systems is not always feasible.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (The rapid advancement of information and communication technology has changed the way traditional systems operate. One of the most important processes in any democratic system is the voting process. Traditionally, voting has been carried out using paper ballots and later with Electronic Voting Machines \(EVMs\). Although these methods have improved the voting process to some extent, they still involve high operational cost, large manpower, and time-consuming procedures. With the growth of internet technologies and web-based applications, the concept of online and digital voting has become popular. A web-based polling booth system provides an efficient, transparent, and easy-to-use platform for conducting elections.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (The Polling Booth System developed in this project is a web-based application created using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. The system makes use of browser Local Storage to store voter details, votes, and results. This allows the system to work without the need for an external database or server. The main purpose of this project is to replace the traditional manual voting method with a simple digital voting system that is suitable for small-scale elections such as college elections, classroom voting, and organizational polls. The system ensures that each user can cast only one vote and that the voting results are generated automatically and instantly.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 143 0 R
/T (1.1 Background Study)
/E (1.1 Background Study)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
