/E (Page No. 02)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Even today, many institutions and organizations use traditional methods for conducting elections, which involve paper ballots or manual processes. These methods suffer from several drawbacks. The voter verification process is slow and sometimes unreliable. Manual counting of votes takes a long time and is prone to mistakes. Maintaining election records on paper is also difficult and insecure. There is always a possibility of duplicate voting, proxy voting, and result manipulation.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (In addition to this, traditional voting systems require physical presence of voters and election officials, which limits accessibility. Conducting elections frequently becomes costly due to the need for printing ballot papers, arranging polling booths, and hiring staff for election duties.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (The problem addressed in this project is to design and develop a simple, cost-effective, and reliable web-based Polling Booth System that can securely handle voter authentication, vote casting, data storage, and result generation using only HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and Local Storage. The system should ensure fairness, transparency, and accuracy in the voting process while being easy to use and maintain.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (The motivation behind developing this Polling Booth System arises from the limitations and challenges faced in the traditional voting process. Manual voting systems require a large number of people for managing voter lists, verifying voter identity, conducting elections, and counting votes. This process becomes highly inefficient, especially when quick and accurate results are required. There is also a risk of human error and vote manipulation, which may affect the transparency of elections.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Another major motivation is the growing demand for digital solutions in every sector. With the increasing use of smartphones, computers, and the internet, people now prefer online systems that are fast, reliable, and easy to use. The idea of developing a web-based polling system using only front-end technologies allows students to understand real-time application development without depending on complex backend servers.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (From an academic point of view, this project also provides hands-on experience in HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and browser-based data storage. It helps students improve their logical thinking, programming skills, and understanding of how real-world systems are designed and implemented using web technologies.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
