393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (The domain of this project is Web Development and Digital Governance Systems, which represents the integration of modern web technologies with digital public service applications. Web development is one of the most rapidly evolving fields in the information technology industry, driven by the increasing demand for online services, digital automation, and internet-based platforms. It involves the design, development, and maintenance of websites and web applications using both front-end and back-end technologies. Front-end development focuses on creating interactive and visually appealing user interfaces using technologies such as HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, while back-end development deals with server-side logic, databases, and security. In this project, the complete system is developed using front-end technologies, making it lightweight, fast, and easy to deploy.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (From the perspective of Digital Governance, the Polling Booth System belongs to the category of E-Governance applications. E-Governance refers to the application of information and communication technologies to deliver government and organizational services in a more efficient, transparent, and accessible manner. Digital governance systems aim to reduce paperwork, minimize human intervention, eliminate corruption, and improve public participation. Online voting and digital polling systems are one of the most important components of E-Governance as they directly involve citizens in the democratic decision-making process. By using a web-based voting platform, the proposed system promotes transparency, accountability, and speed in election management.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
396 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (This project also contributes to the domain of Digital Democracy, where technology is used to support democratic processes such as voting, opinion polling, and public decision-making. Traditional voting systems often face challenges like low voter turnout, slow result processing, and high operational costs. By contrast, a web-based polling system offers instant voting, automated result generation, and improved accessibility. Even though the current system is designed for small-scale use, it reflects the broader vision of how digital platforms can transform democratic practices in the future.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
