403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 149 0 R
/T (METHODOLOGY)
/E (METHODOLOGY)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (The existing voting system is mostly based on manual or semi-automated processes. In many institutions, voting is carried out using paper ballots where voters mark their choice and place the ballot in a ballot box. After the voting process is completed, the ballots are collected and counted manually. This process takes a lot of time and is vulnerable to errors such as miscounting, invalid votes, and manipulation.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (In some cases, Electronic Voting Machines are used, which reduce the time required for counting votes. However, these machines are expensive and require technical staff for setup and maintenance. They also require physical presence of voters at polling stations. Overall, the existing system is not fully efficient and lacks flexibility, especially for small organizations and institutions that conduct frequent elections.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (The methodology adopted for developing the Polling Booth System follows a systematic approach to software development. The project begins with the analysis of requirements to understand the needs of users and the functional scope of the system. After this, the system design phase involves planning the layout, navigation flow, and data handling structure of the application.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (The next phase is the implementation stage, where HTML is used to create the basic structure of the web pages, CSS is used to design the layout and improve the visual appearance, and JavaScript is used to implement the core logic of the system. Local Storage is integrated into the project to store voter details, candidate information, and voting results. After implementation, the system undergoes thorough testing to ensure that all functionalities work correctly and that there are no errors in vote storage and result calculation. Finally, the system is evaluated based on its performance, reliability, and user experience.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 149 0 R
/T (4.1 Existing System)
/E (4.1 Existing System)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
409 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 149 0 R
/T (4.2 Proposed System)
/E (4.2 Proposed System)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (The proposed Polling Booth System is a fully web-based application that allows users to cast their votes digitally using a web browser. Unlike traditional systems, this system does not require any physical voting infrastructure or external database servers. All data related to voters, candidates, and votes is stored securely in the browser using Local Storage.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
