416 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (The system provides a simple login mechanism to verify users before allowing them to vote. Once the voter is authenticated, the system displays a list of candidates, and the voter can select their preferred candidate. After the vote is submitted, the system records the vote and ensures that the same user cannot vote again. The results are automatically calculated and can be viewed instantly by the administrator.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 150 0 R
/T (4.3 Objective of the Project)
/E (4.3 Objective of the Project)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
418 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (The main objective of this project is to provide a reliable and easy-to-use digital voting system that can be used for small-scale elections. The project aims to reduce the time and effort required to conduct elections and to ensure fair and transparent voting. It also focuses on eliminating duplicate voting and manual errors in vote counting. Another key objective is to help students gain practical experience in developing real-time web applications using front-end technologies and browser-based storage.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
