426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (The system is required to provide a secure login for users, display the list of candidates, allow the user to cast their vote, and store the vote securely using Local Storage. It must prevent duplicate voting and provide an admin interface for viewing and managing election results. The system should also be compatible with different web browsers and devices.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Requirement analysis is one of the most important phases of software development. It involves identifying and documenting the needs and expectations of users. For the Polling Booth System, the requirements are divided into system requirements, functional requirements, and non-functional requirements. The system must be able to handle user authentication, vote casting, vote storage, and result generation in a secure and reliable manner.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 151 0 R
/T (5.1 System Requirement Specification)
/E (5.1 System Requirement Specification)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 151 0 R
/T (5.2 Software Specifications)
/E (5.2 Software Specifications)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (The Polling Booth System can run on any operating system such as Windows, Linux, or macOS. The development environment requires a web browser such as Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, or Microsoft Edge. The system is developed using HTML for structure, CSS for styling, and JavaScript for logic implementation. A simple code editor such as Visual Studio Code or Notepad++ can be used for development.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 151 0 R
/T (5.1.1 Non-Functional Requirements)
/E (5.1.1 Non-Functional Requirements)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (The Polling Booth System should provide a user-friendly interface that is easy to understand even for first-time users. The system should respond quickly to user actions and ensure smooth navigation between pages. It must be reliable and free from errors during the voting process. Data stored in Local Storage should be consistent and protected from accidental loss. The system should also be scalable for handling a reasonable number of users during an election.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 151 0 R
/T (5.1.2 Functional Requirements)
/E (5.1.2 Functional Requirements)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
434 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (The system should allow users to register or log in before voting. After successful authentication, the system should display the available candidates. The user should be able to select one candidate and submit their vote. Once the vote is submitted, the system should store the vote in Local Storage and prevent the user from voting again. The admin should be able to view the total votes received by each candidate and display the final election results.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
