>>
endobj
800 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 162 0 R
/E (The main algorithm of the system begins when the user logs into the application. The system first checks whether the user has already voted. If the user has not voted, the system allows them to proceed to the voting page. After the user selects a candidate and submits their vote, the system stores the vote in Local Storage and marks the user as having voted. The result is then updated by increasing the vote count of the selected candidate. This algorithm ensures fairness and prevents duplicate voting. The techniques used in this project include client-side validation, event-driven programming using JavaScript, and browser-based data storage.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
801 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 162 0 R
/E (The sequence diagram represents the order of interactions between different components of the system. When the user opens the website, the system displays the login page. After the user enters valid credentials, the system verifies the user and grants access to the voting page. The user selects a candidate and submits the vote. The system stores the vote and updates the result. Finally, the admin accesses the result page to view the final outcome of the election.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
802 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 162 0 R
/T (6.2 Algorithm and Technique)
/E (6.2 Algorithm and Technique)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
